            <ArticleTitle>Venepuncture: best practice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-65; quiz 66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Venepuncture is the introduction of a needle into a vein to obtain a blood sample for haematological, biochemical or bacteriological analysis. It is the most common invasive procedure undertaken in hospital. This article provides guidance on the theory and practice of venepuncture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
